From 4c715ae06d0a95c15445c27dd3357faf1d3f4d90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:45:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Todo Task as 10th generic section (SQLite + Express +
 React)

- todo_task + todo_task_history tables in home_dashboard_schema.sql
  (the only schema file actually loaded at boot), with a trigger that
  auto-logs status changes for report generation and keeps updated_at
  current -- no application code needed for either.
- Register todo_task in backend/db/sectionConfig.js. No changes needed
  to routes/sections.js or db/sectionRepository.js -- both were already
  fully generic.
- Add todo_task to frontend/src/config/sectionFields.js: a short
  quick-add "fields" set plus a new "detailFields" key (extra columns
  shown only on the View All page). detailFields is additive and
  optional -- existing sections are unaffected.
- Generalize components/SectionForm.jsx to accept a "fieldsOverride"
  prop instead of always reading config.fields, so a fuller field list
  can reuse the same generic form (backward compatible).
- New components/SectionDetailView.jsx: a generic 'View all' page
  (table + add/edit/delete) driven entirely by sectionFields.js, so any
  section gets a working detail view for free. Replaces the one-off,
  non-generic scenes/routine/RoutineAdmin.jsx as the reusable pattern
  (that file is left in place/untouched).
- New components/SectionQuickAdd.jsx: standalone page version of the
  quick-add modal, for deep-linking (e.g. /todo-task/new).
- Wire /todo-task and /todo-task/new routes in App.js.
- scenes/dashboard/index.jsx: add todo_task as a 10th grid card (no
  10-section limit exists -- CSS grid auto-flows), plus a generic
  date-range/status/category/priority filter row for any section that
  declares "dashboardFilter" in sectionFields.js. No such filter
  pattern existed before this change.
- scenes/global/BottomNav.jsx: '+' now opens the Todo Task quick-add
  (generic SectionForm) instead of the old category-based AddTaskForm.
  AddTask.jsx and its /add-task route are left fully intact for future
  use -- only the bottom-nav entry point was repointed.
